      "groovy_code": "process abricate {\n    input:\n      tuple val(riscd_input), path(scaffolds), val(database)\n    output:\n      path '*'\n      tuple val(riscd), path(\"${base}_vdabricate_calls.txt\"), emit: calls\n      path '*.sh', hidden: true\n    script:\n      md = parseMetadataFromFileName(scaffolds.getName())\n      base = \"${md.ds}-${ex.dt}_${md.cmp}\"\n      riscd = getRisCd(md, ex, STEP, METHOD)\n      \"\"\"\n        abricate ${scaffolds} --datadir ${abricateDBDir} -db ${database} &>> ${base}_vdabricate.log >> ${base}_vdabricate_calls.txt\n      \"\"\"\n}",
      "caveats": [
        "The `scaffolds.getName()` method assumes the input is a single file. If the channel emits a list of files, this will fail.",
        "The `md` object structure must match the output of `parseMetadataFromFileName`. Any mismatch will cause runtime errors.",
        "The `riscd` variable must be defined in the script block before it is used in the output tuple. Nextflow does not allow forward references in output declarations.",
        "The `base` variable is used in both the script and output declarations, so any changes to its construction must be consistent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "combining_a_channel_with_a_static_list",
      "title": "Combining a Channel with a Static List",
      "description": "This pattern shows how to use the `.combine()` operator to merge a channel with a static list. This is particularly useful when you need to pair each element from a dynamic channel with a fixed set of values (e.g., database names, parameters).",
