    {
      "id": "conditional_tuple_unpacking_with_metadata_parsing",
      "title": "Conditional Tuple Unpacking with Metadata Parsing",
      "description": "This pattern demonstrates how to unpack a tuple input conditionally and parse metadata from the file name within the process script. It is particularly useful when dealing with paired-end reads where the file structure needs to be dynamically handled based on the input type.",
      "use_cases": [
        "Handling paired-end and single-end reads in the same process",
        "Dynamic metadata extraction from file names for downstream processing",
        "Conditional logic for file compression handling"
      ],
      "groovy_code": "process kraken2 {\n    input:\n      tuple val(riscd_input), path(reads)\n    script:\n      (t1,t2) = reads\n      md = parseMetadataFromFileName(t1.getName())\n      base = \"${md.ds}-${ex.dt}_${md.cmp}\"\n      options = isIlluminaPaired(reads) ? ' --paired ' : ''\n      options += t1.getName().endsWith(\".gz\") ? \" --gzip-compressed \" : \"\"\n      \"\"\"\n        kraken2 --db ${KRAKEN2_DB} --threads 64 ${options} ${t1} ${t2} --output ${base}_kraken.txt --report ${base}_kraken.tsv 2> ${base}_kraken.log\n        gzip ${base}_kraken.txt\n      \"\"\"\n}",
      "caveats": [
        "Ensure that the tuple unpacking matches the structure of the input channel. Mismatched tuple sizes will cause runtime errors.",
        "The `parseMetadataFromFileName` function must be robust to handle various file naming conventions.",
        "Conditional logic for file compression must accurately detect the file extension to avoid incorrect handling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "multi_output_channel_emission",
      "title": "Multi-Output Channel Emission",
      "description": "This pattern shows how to emit multiple outputs from a process using named channels. It is useful when a single process generates multiple types of outputs that need to be handled separately in downstream processes.",
      "use_cases": [
        "Generating multiple report files from a single process",
        "Separating log files from result files for different publishing directories",
        "Emitting different types of data for downstream analysis"
