    {
      "id": "conditional_schema_resolution_with_fallback_logic",
      "title": "Conditional Schema Resolution with Fallback Logic",
      "description": "This pattern demonstrates how to resolve a schema based on genus/species information with fallback logic. It first checks for an exact match of genus_species, then falls back to genus-only matching, and finally defaults to the first allowed schema if no specific schema is provided.",
      "use_cases": [
        "When working with taxonomic data where species-level schemas may not always be available",
        "For pipelines that need to handle both specific and general taxonomic classifications",
        "When you need to provide sensible defaults while still allowing for specific overrides"
      ],
      "groovy_code": "def getSchema(gsp, schema) {\n  try {\n    def genus_species = gsp ? gsp.toLowerCase() : ''\n    def (genus, species) = genus_species.contains(\"_\") ? genus_species.split('_') : [ genus_species, null ]\n\n    def allowedSchemas = []\n    if (SPECIES_SCHEMA.containsKey(genus_species)) {\n      allowedSchemas =  SPECIES_SCHEMA.get(genus_species)\n    } else if (SPECIES_SCHEMA.containsKey(genus)) {\n      allowedSchemas = SPECIES_SCHEMA.get(genus)\n    }\n    if (!allowedSchemas) {\n      log.debug \"no compatible schemas found for genus_species: ${genus_species}\"\n      return null\n    }\n    if (!schema) {\n      return allowedSchemas[0] //at this stage, use the first allowed schema\n    }\n    if (allowedSchemas.contains(schema)) {\n      return schema\n    }\n    log.warn \"schema ${schema} not compatible with genus_species: ${genus_species}\"\n    return null;\n  } catch(Throwable t) {\n      exit 1, \"unexpected exception: ${t.asString()}\"\n  }\n}",
      "caveats": [
        "The split operation assumes genus_species follows the pattern 'genus_species' with exactly one underscore",
        "Returns null if no compatible schema is found, which requires proper null handling in calling code",
        "The fallback to allowedSchemas[0] assumes the list is non-empty, which is checked but should be documented",
        "Case sensitivity in schema names must be consistent throughout the pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "parameterized_conditional_processing_based_on_sequencing_tec",
      "title": "Parameterized Conditional Processing Based on Sequencing Technology",
      "description": "This pattern shows how to conditionally select processing parameters based on sequencing technology (Ion Torrent vs others) while maintaining a clean separation of configuration data. It uses lookup tables for different sequencing technologies and provides appropriate fallback behavior.",
      "use_cases": [
