    {
      "id": "cross_with_key_extraction_and_multimap_for_tuple_deconstruct",
      "title": "Cross with Key Extraction and MultiMap for Tuple Deconstruction",
      "description": "This pattern demonstrates how to cross two channels (reads and reference), apply a key extraction function to the resulting tuples, and then use multiMap to deconstruct the tuples into named channels. This is particularly useful when you need to associate reads with multiple reference attributes (e.g., RISC ID, code, path) while maintaining a clean channel structure for downstream processes.",
